// fetch_workdrive_text.dg — downloads a WorkDrive file's raw text content by file id (resource_id
// — see ../shared/upload_workdrive_json.dg's header for that field's confirmed real name/shape).
//
// Used to read large text blobs (house-rules docs) that are too big to fit in a CRM org
// variable — org variables have a real size ceiling well below a several-hundred-line policy
// doc, hit live while trying to store Digest_house_rules_sales_manager as plain text. The org
// variable now holds only the short WorkDrive file id (Digest_house_rules_<profile>_file_id);
// the actual text lives in a WorkDrive .txt file and is fetched fresh here on every
// digest_generate_<profile>.dg call — this is still cheap relative to the Claude call itself,
// and the house-rules TEXT (not this fetch) is what Anthropic's cache_control caches across
// days, so re-fetching daily doesn't undo that savings.
//
// Confirmed live, in order, before landing on this version:
//  - invokeurl GET to download.zoho.com/v1/workdrive/download/<id> with
//    connection:"workdrive_connection" — 401 (wrong host for this Connection).
//  - zoho.workdrive.downloadFile(fileId, connection), guessed as a native counterpart to
//    ../shared/upload_digest.dg's working zoho.workdrive.uploadFile — not a real Deluge task.
//  - Same GET against www.zohoapis.com/workdrive/api/v1/download/<id> instead — fixes the 401,
//    but the file was uploaded with a .jsonl extension, which WorkDrive serves back as
//    content-type: application/x-unknown; invokeurl can't expose that as text (plain call's
//    .toString() empty, detailed:true's responseText just the filename).
//  - Tried iterating the response with `for each` (Deluge does support this for File objects) —
//    real feature, but CSV-only: "'.csv file formats are only supported to iterate.'" Confirms
//    fileResp genuinely is a Deluge File object, and that Deluge's file-content handling is
//    keyed off recognized type/extension.
// Fix: every WorkDrive upload this repo makes for text meant to be read back this way now uses a
// .txt filename instead of an arbitrary one, so WorkDrive serves it back as text/plain — a
// content-type invokeurl exposes as plain text through this function's .toString() call below.
// .json was tried for the pending-batch state (generate/digest_generate.dg — genuinely one valid
// JSON object, so it seemed like the "correct" label) but hit "Invalid JSON Format String" live
// on the caller's later .toMap() call, most likely because invokeurl auto-parses an
// application/json response into a Map internally, and re-serializing that via this function's
// .toString() then re-parsing again apparently doesn't round-trip cleanly for that content — so
// every caller now uses .txt uniformly (house-rules docs, pending-batch state, and the
// batch-results relay in generate/digest_finish_batches.dg, which is genuinely JSONL and was
// .txt from the start for a related reason: avoiding that same auto-parse path on invalid JSON).

string standalone.fetchWorkdriveText(String fileId)
{
	response = invokeurl
	[
		url: "https://www.zohoapis.com/workdrive/api/v1/download/" + fileId
		type: GET
		connection: "workdrive_connection"
	];
	return response.toString();
}
